==French==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|fr}} {{term|amuser||to amuse, divert|lang=frm}}, from {{etyl|fro|fr}} {{term|amuser||to stupefy|lang=fro}}, from {{term|a-|lang=fro}} + {{term|muser||to stare stupidly at, be bewildered|lang=fro}}. {{term||Muser|lang=fro}} is possibly from {{term|mus||snout|lang=fro}}, which is from {{etyl|ML.|fr}} {{term|musum|lang=la}} of {{etyl|gem|fr}} origin; or, possibly from {{etyl|frk|-}} *{{term|masjan|masjan, musōn|to stun, confuse, confound|lang=frk}}, from {{proto|Germanic|mas-|to confuse, stun, delay|lang=fr}}. In the latter case, akin to {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|amasian|āmasian|to confuse, stupefy, bewilder|lang=ang}} (whence {{etyl|en|-}} {{term|amaze|lang=en}}), {{etyl|non|-}} {{term|masa||to struggle, be confused|lang=non}} (whence {{etyl|nor|-}} {{term|mas||exhausting labour|lang=nor}} and {{term|masast||to be dazed, begin to dream|lang=nor}}, and {{etyl|swe|-}} {{term|masa||to dawdle, idle|lang=swe}} and {{term|mos||sluggish|sleepy|lang=swe}}). See also {{term|amaze|lang=en}}.

